10:    Input structure:
11:    - Grid contains several colored square frames (hollow borders of a single color).
12:    - Each frame's interior holds a small pattern sprite; one frame's interior is blank (all black).
13:    - Two frames form a training pair (their interiors share the same color palette); one remaining frame is the test case.
14:
15:    Rule:
16:    - Identify the training pair by matching interior color sets; the other non-blank frame is the test input.
17:    - Infer the rule mapping source→destination (e.g. reflection, color inversion, gap filling, endpoint extraction, or checkerboard complement).
18:    - Apply that same rule to the test sprite; output the transformed interior.
19:
20:    Key insight: The puzzle is an analogy — "A is to B as C is to ?" — where you must discover the visual rule from one example pair and generalize it.
